<div class="text guide-styles" data-units-dynamic="article" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">
<div class="markup-toc-wrapper">
<button class="markup-toc-button">Show Table of Contents</button></div>Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid Tank in Cataclysm Classic Phase 4. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Dragon Soul, Firelands, Twilight Protocol Dungeons, and Valor Points. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="gearing-philosophy">
<span class="c11"> Feral Druid Tank Gearing Philosophy</span></h2>
<span class="c11">
<span class="icontiny" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif");'>Feral Druid Tank</span></span> gearing is not straightforward, it depends heavily on what you're doing for your raid as a <span class="c11">
<span class="icontiny" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif");'>Feral Druid Tank</span></span>. <span class="c11">
<span class="icontiny" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif");'>Feral Druids</span></span> can do <i>everything</i> from Main-Tanking to Off-Tanking to DPSing, and even all these roles in the same encounter. Most <span class="c11">
<span class="icontiny" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif");'>Feral Druid Tanks</span></span> however will be in the same situation that you're there to help the Main Tank with the Tank mechanics and use downtime to DPS in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=768/cat-form">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>There is not one single path for <span class="c11">
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif");'>Feral Druid Tanks</span></span>. For some full survivability might be the correct gearing option and for some going full offensive might be the correct gearing option, it all depends on you, your raid group, the gear available to you, your assignments, what content you're aiming to clear, etc. <i>
<b>There's a wide spectrum, and it is unlikely that being on the far end of either side is the best thing for you and your raid group</b></i> so make gearing adjustments from any list below that fits within the context of how you approach the game.<br/>
<br/>Due to <span class="c11">
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif");'>Feral Druid Tank</span></span> gearing being so flexible, I've put together multiple Best in Slot lists based on these <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/druid/feral/tank-stat-priority-attributes-pve">Stat Priorities</a>. As a general rule of thumb however, <b>
<i>if you're new to the raid, go as defensive as you can</i></b>. Being tanky allows your raid to make more mistakes, which there will always be before your raid group is comfortable with the fights, once you and they are comfortable you can start looking into going more offensive.<br/>
<br/>
<i>Why shouldn't I always just go full defensive as a <span class="c11">
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif");'>Feral Druid Tank</span></span>?</i> In Cataclysm you can enter a raid for the first time with good enough gear to clear the content, the previous Tier's Best in Slot gear with full Defensive focus will be worse defensively than the current Tier's gear with full Offensive focus. On top of that, you and your raid group will get more comfortable and your Healers will get better gear. In reality, it all comes down to how you want to play the game, but you being able to survive while putting out damage will end up making your raids faster and smoother.<br/>
<br/>Try to be the kind of player who looks to improve, talk to your healers if you're uncertain whether you could drop some defensive stats, and utilize your raid's and your own defensive cooldowns! <br/>
<br/>
<b>The offensive sets below are FULL offensive with no regard to surviving, they <ins>can</ins> be used on some bosses, but that doesn't mean they necessarily should be used.</b> You're still a tank and surviving should always be your priority number 1.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c11">Best in Slot Gear for Feral Druid Tank Phase 4</span></h2>
