<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="tier-bonuses-in-firelands">
<span class="c11">Tier Bonuses in Firelands</span></h3>For <span class="c11">
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif");'>Feral Druid Tanks</span></span> there luckily isn't any doubt in what set bonuses to choose as we only have 1 to choose from. However, with the access to LFR tier, you might have to early on choose between the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-351/obsidian-arborweave-battlegarb">Tier 12 set bonuses</a> and the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-499/deep-earth-battlegarb">Tier 13 set bonuses</a> without any massive change in stats between the 2 sets. It is not worth to break <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-351/obsidian-arborweave-battlegarb">4-set Tier 12</a> for either the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-480/deep-earth-battlegarb">LFR 2-set Tier 13</a> or <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-429/cataclysmic-gladiators-sanctuary">PVP 2-set Season 11</a>.<br/>When it comes to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-351/obsidian-arborweave-battlegarb">Heroic 4-set Tier 12</a> vs <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-480/deep-earth-battlegarb">LFR 4-set Tier 13</a> it becomes a bit more difficult as the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-480/deep-earth-battlegarb">Tier 13 set</a> doesn't benefit us, it might even hurt our survivability as one of our main defensive abilities turn into one of if not the strongest raid defensive cooldown. <br/>It turns into a discussion of raid survivability versus personal survivability, as running <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-351/obsidian-arborweave-battlegarb">Heroic 4-set Tier 12</a> is ~5% less damage taken compared to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-480/deep-earth-battlegarb">LFR 4-set Tier 13</a>. It will depend on what boss you're fighting as some are more scary for you and some are more scary for the raid, the bosses I think you might want to prioritize for your own survivability are <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=56427/warmaster-blackhorn">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Warmaster Blackhorn</span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=56173/deathwing">Madness of Deathwing</a> but these fights also have a lot of raid damage taken, so talk to your raid leader about it.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Feral Druid Tank</h3>
